---
description: Repository conventions for authoring and maintaining Agent Toolkit plugins and host adapters.
alwaysApply: true
---

Read AGENTS.md for repository boundaries and quality gates. Keep canonical
skills, agents, commands, and executable projects inside their owning plugin.

Claude, Codex, and Cursor marketplace registrations must resolve to the same
plugin directories and agree on plugin names and versions. Host metadata is
not a second implementation tree.

Native projections under .opencode/, .copilot/, and .antigravity/ are generated
and ignored. Change their canonical source or Python adapter, never the output.
Run focused harness tests and generation checks after changing host adapters.

Preserve read-only MCP and quality-agent boundaries. Do not port Claude hooks,
register MCP servers, change user settings, or install globally without an
explicit request. Test installers against temporary targets and use dry runs.
